\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. There is a green hill far away,
\par Without a city wall,
\par Where the dear Lord was crucified
\par Who died to save us all.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. We may not know, we cannot tell
\par What pains He had to bear;
\par But we believe it was for us
\par He hung and suffered there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. He died that we might be forgiven,
\par He died to make us good,
\par That we might go at last to heaven
\par Saved by His precious blood.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. There was no other good enough
\par To pay the price of sin;
\par He only could unlock the gate
\par Of heaven, and let us in.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O dearly, dearly has He loved,
\par And we must love Him too,
\par And trust in His redeeming blood,
\par And try His works to do.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

